A||||25||JohnF||"Pretty" car||||6||
Z||000000||JohnF||12-07-2001||07:55 AM||||Went thru a Christmas drive-thru last evening.  All cars lined up for miles.  <P>I was told at the end of the drive that the director squawked "Hold all cars after the pretty little red one without the roof to get some space."<P>I looked behind me and there wasn't another car in sight!<P>I just love to hear what others think about our cars.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001112&p=56509969&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||6
Z||000001||842m8||12-07-2001||04:03 PM||||I know what you mean!<BR>I was at a stop light and there were a few guys walking across the street and all their heads were stuck on my car and one guy said "Whoa.... a Ferrari!" I just kinda chuckled<BR>I especially love the looks I get driving around, last night a guy in a little Swift I think it was a turbo too he comes flying up beside me and he's looking at my car then he looks at me and smiles.... it was hillarious<p>[This message has been edited by 842m8 (edited 12-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||JD86GT350||12-07-2001||07:02 PM||||the last time I had my GT out, I went past a new black firebird that was pulling out of a gas station.  He got on it, and pulled up next to me slowed down, gave me a big "ok" symbol then turned right.  It sure put a big grin on my face too   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||JohnF||12-07-2001||07:08 PM||||Yeah!  <P>Most of the people that see our cars don't have a clue what they are.  Think about the fact that a 20 y.o. was 6 or 7 when the last car rolled off the line!!!   It was designed and delivered almost before he(she) was born! <P>Maybe this thread should be  "What have you heard?"<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001112&p=56509969&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||10
Z||000004||avengador1||12-07-2001||07:50 PM||||I know the feeling. Last weekend I went to Home Depot and when I was leaving I noticed this couple stopped in their tracks looking at my car as I left. You'd think they were looking at a Ferrari. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||banditbalz||12-07-2001||08:11 PM||||Let's face it, all affordable cars today are boring in design. Take the Acura RSX for example. It's admired by every 16 yr old kid walking around with his pants hang'n down to his knees, but it has no style. Does anybody here, think this car stands out in a parking lot? And why is it that if I go to the mall for 30 minutes, park at the farthest, most remote parking spot I can find, somebody just has to park beside me. Sometimes I come out to find a crowd of people drooling. And just imagine what would happen if I actually put any money into this car...<P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||12
Z||000006||artherd||12-07-2001||09:03 PM||||"So, what kind of Porsche is that?"<P>"Nice Ferrari!"<P>I love this car!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000007||My7Fieros||12-07-2001||09:19 PM||||Get this......yesterday I was trailoring my red 86 SE (parts car!) to the Fiero Factory (traded for work, long story). Anyway I was in Corinth, MS and had a flat on the trailor. I took it to a Gateway Tire store to replace the tire. Every one of those guys in there gathered around the Fiero on the trailor and we're literally in awe. They were asking all kinds of questions about it. Keep in mind, this thing was a BEATER! It was my parts car...had badly faded paint, NO hood, smashed windshield, ect...but these guys (who somewhat resembled the characters in the movie "Deliverance") were in love with it. I answered all their questions of course. When I left, my friend and I cracked up.........(I thought I heard "Dueling Banjos" playing in the background!)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||7
Z||000008||88-DOHC||12-07-2001||10:24 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by banditbalz:<BR><B>Let's face it, all affordable cars today are boring in design. Take the Acura RSX for example. It's admired by every 16 yr old kid walking around with his pants hang'n down to his knees, but it has no style. Does anybody here, think this car stands out in a parking lot? And why is it that if I go to the mall for 30 minutes, park at the farthest, most remote parking spot I can find, somebody just has to park beside me. Sometimes I come out to find a crowd of people drooling. And just imagine what would happen if I actually put any money into this car...<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>When they first came out I thought the RSX was a good design. However now days they are just plain boring... Why?  Because there are millions of them on the road, so they have lost the uniqueness they once had. However that doesn't stop people (ricers) from adoring them.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <P>The main reason I got into Fiero's in the first place, was because they looked good, have a fair amount of upgrade options (largely due to the kitcar industry) and are basicly unique.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Well, they are more unique in some parts of the world then others. Around here, there is more then 2 on the road. I see them fairly often on the road.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||4BanGinFun||12-07-2001||11:10 PM||||im a 17 yr old guy with an 85 se the day my dad brought it home i thought it was a ferrari! then he told me its a pontiac i fell in love right then and there! <P>here in Canada they are a very rare car! your lucky if you see 2 of them in the same day on the road kind of sux for buying a nice one (no fastbacks where i am   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> ) and they all seem to be 4cyl and '84s but they still  do turn heads <P><BR>edit for spelling<BR>------------------<BR>85 se 2m4 5spd white<P> <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/super/camaro0/" TARGET=_blank>www.angelfire.com/super/camaro0/</A> <p>[This message has been edited by 4BanGinFun (edited 12-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||Formula||12-08-2001||07:12 AM||||I had some guy get pissed off at me because I was putting a can of gas in the pasenger seat (for the tractor) of my "lotus".  Then I just told him it was my beater car and tore out of there.<P>I've had a lot of little kids call it a Ferrari and a lot of older guys cal it a lotus..... If you know what a lotus is then you should know what a fiero is, right?||||reg||1
Z||000011||JohnF||12-08-2001||07:31 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 4BanGinFun:<BR><B>your lucky if you see 2 of them in the same day <BR>edit for spelling</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I live in the Dallas/Ft. Worth metroplex area that takes up all of north central Texas.  I feel I am lucky if I see another Fiero on the road 2 times in a MONTH.  <P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001112&p=56509969&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||6
Z||000012||SLAMMED87GT||12-08-2001||11:26 AM||||Ohh boyyy!!!! I could tell you so many stories of what people have done just to see my car better!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>I've gotten plenty of the "Is that a new Lotus" lines. Makes me feel good!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Even the ricers will come up to me and be like, "Cool ride yo!" We don't have as many ricers here and they want someone else with a cool car to like hang out with! Even a guy with an automatic Prelude wanted me to join him and some other ricers to drag race!<P>One night after I had come home from a car show (in which I had gotten a trophy, which was propped up behind the passenger seat), I was parked at the gas station. This ghetto black dude is just looking at my car and smiling and doing some type of hooptie dance by my car! He's talking to his white girlfriend and he goes "Ahh man, he's even got a trophy and sh!t. That is so tight!"<P>It was pretty cool......... :P<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pfierosig2_1.jpg">  <P>------------------<BR>3" Drop, 17" Primax 618s/Nitto450 205/40, 4" Monza exhaust, Mudstain decklid scoop, 7" wing stands, Clear front and rear lights, custom interior, all options...that's all hehe.<P>[This message has been edited by SLAMMED87GT (edited 12-08-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by SLAMMED87GT (edited 12-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||Brandon86SE||12-08-2001||12:07 PM||||I got more stories than this, but shortly after I bought my car I had it parked at school, I was in grade 12 at the time, and I came out at the end of the day to see a crowd of grade 9/10's around my car.  They were looking in the windows checking out the interior and stuff, but not one of them had the nerve to actually touch it.  I just walked right up to the car, nodded my head at them, opened the door, and took off (fast!)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Had a big grin on my face for a couple days!  Stuff like that makes me love my car!<P>Brandon<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000014||88-DOHC||12-08-2001||02:48 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula:<BR><B>I've had a lot of little kids call it a Ferrari and a lot of older guys cal it a lotus..... If you know what a lotus is then you should know what a fiero is, right?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You would think that would be the case.  Oh well, here in Northen California, people actually see things like Lotus's, Lambo's and Ferrari's on the roads once in a while, so I guess that lowers the mystique of the Feiro a bit. To top it off ricers are a dime a dozen here.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> At least I don't have to worry about while adding my own uniques to my car, making it look like every other car on the road in the process.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000015||fierochild||12-08-2001||07:24 PM||||Last Sunday, as I was leaving an autocross at Turner Field in Hotlanta, I pulled up to a stop light and this guy says to his friend "Hey check out the Ferrari." <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Also, I just got a paint code for my here-to-fore custom paint job.  It seem Lamborghini thinks the color is cool also.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">  Check out the cover of the December issue of Automobile magazine.  I love this car man.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>Chuck<BR>Lambo green 86GT<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierochildsig_1.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by fierochild (edited 12-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000016||Jaei Sun||12-08-2001||08:19 PM||||Chuck,<P>I love that color!!  Got any more pictures of your car... maybe some high res ones!!!<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://home.mn.rr.com/fierojaei/Jaei_blue.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||Tina||12-09-2001||12:10 PM||||One thing that happens quite often,there I'am<BR>sitting at the stop light just waiting my turn.<BR>Left or right lane,(take your pick)people actually stop behind me in the other lane, not because of standing traffic ahead of them,<BR>(we are talking up to 4 or 5 car lengths ahead of them in open space)<BR>and then inch forward <B>inch by inch</B>.<P>What's wrong with these people.<BR>Never seen a Fiero?<P>Tina  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000018||Formula||12-09-2001||01:52 PM||||Tina: its either 1 of 2 things...<P>1. They are afraid your going to suck them up through your deck scoop.<P>2. because of the fieros rep. people might think its going to catch on fire.<P>I vote for 1 myself.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000019||fldevel||12-09-2001||02:08 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tina:<BR><B>One thing that happens quite often,there I'am<BR>sitting at the stop light just waiting my turn.<BR>Left or right lane,(take your pick)people actually stop behind me in the other lane, not because of standing traffic ahead of them,<BR>(we are talking up to 4 or 5 car lengths ahead of them in open space)<BR>and then inch forward [b]inch by inch</B>.<P>What's wrong with these people.<BR>Never seen a Fiero?<P>Tina   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>maybe its not the fiero there looking at??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000020||fierochild||12-09-2001||03:22 PM||||Jaei Sun,<BR>    I've tried several times to get a decent photo of my car without success.  I've tried a cheapy digital, a Polaroid, and one of the wedding throw-away cameras.  All of the resulted in color wash out.  I finally drug out my old (read 1960s vintage) Pentax K1000.  It's at the shop being tuned up.  As soon as I get it back I'll try again.  With that thing I have several filters and light settings to play with.  Maybe then I can come up with a good photo.  If so I'll post it to the list for all to see.<P>Thanks for asking<BR>Chuck<BR>Lambo Green 86 GT<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierochildsig_1.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by fierochild (edited 12-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000021||842m8||12-09-2001||04:51 PM||||There are a few Fieros here in Cambridge but you're lucky if you see them once a month there is a SWEET silver one here with a double deck shopping kart wing, I make fun of those on ricers but it actually looks amazing on this fask back fiero! anyways me and my brother have 3 Fieros... 1 mint condition one stored in the garage and 2 we drive, anyways one day we were going out for dinner with our parents, me and my brother took our Fieros because we were going out right after so we're driving down the road behind each other and this riced out Del Sol with flames and graphics all over it litterally stopped in the middle of the road and I seen his head follow us as we drove past him in the oppisite direstion hahaha it was awesome!<BR><p>[This message has been edited by 842m8 (edited 12-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000022||Heretic||12-09-2001||05:03 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 842m8:<BR><B>There are a few Fieros here in Cambridge but you're lucky if you see them once a month there is a SWEET silver one here with a double deck shopping kart wing, I make fun of those on ricers but it actually looks amazing on this fask back fiero! anyways me and my brother have 3 Fieros... 1 mint condition one stored in the garage and 2 we drive, anyways one day we were going out for dinner with our parents, me and my brother took our Fieros because we were going out right after so we're driving down the road behind each other and this riced out Del Sol with flames and graphics all over it litterally stopped in the middle of the road and I seen his head follow us as we drove past him in the oppisite direstion hahaha it was awesome!<P><BR>[This message has been edited by 842m8 (edited 12-09-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Your from Cambridge! Sweet! I see that Del Sol like every day at school , nothin special. Ugly paint and a park bench , bah! Have you seen my brothers 86 GT around?(one in my sig) What does your Fiero look like , just incase i see you around somewhere? Theres about 6 or 7 nice ones i've seen around here , yours may be one of them   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>EDIT: The silver one you mentioned is one of the mechanics cars from Evans Racing Products. I'm pretty sure its on Sheldon Drive in the same plaza as Radworld. The rims he has on it arent too bad either..<P>------------------<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/hereticsig_1.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Heretic (edited 12-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000023||Jncomutt||12-09-2001||06:22 PM||||When I was in Boston 2 weeks ago, I pulled my car up to the front of Dicks last resort.  So as I'm waitin for my friend to come out, I hear this kid quitely say to his friend, damn thats a sexy car.  Well they keep takin quick looks at it as they walk by, noticing i'm watching them.  Then when they get all the way by it, He goes "Holy, Sh.., Thats a F..kin' Fiero??  He then walked back to the pass. window to ask what year it was and to say 'nice ride'   Makes me feel good...||||reg||1
